❝
When whisky is stored in barrels for maturation, approximately 2% of the liquid evaporates per year. This is called the ‘Angel’s Share’ as this portion of liquid gold seemingly disappears into the heavens. It keeps the angels in good spirits.
❞
– Wikipedia, Facts about Whiskey
❝
One of the main reasons for the past unpopularity of rum has been due to the lack of knowledge about the various types to be used, its various flavors and its proper use. No one bothers to explain that there is a rum for every purpose.
❞
– Trader Vic, Book of Food and Drink, 1946
❝
After Sir Francis Chichester became the first man to successfully circumnavigate the world solo in a sailboat, he credits his success to a daily glass of Pink Gin (gin, Angostura bitters and cold water), and said the saddest day was when the gin ran out.
❞
– Jared Brown, 50 Surprising & Delightful Gin Facts
